{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"a1","type":"claim","text":"The repeated pattern of agreeing and later disagreeing about what the agreement meant indicates underspecified, unrecorded agreements — a shared-memory failure — rather than, on the material given, evidence of bad faith.","grounds":"The task reports agreements whose meaning diverges afterward.","scope":"Household chore coordination"},{"id":"a2","type":"claim","text":"Fixed chore allocations have an implicit expiry date when work schedules change; recurring arguments may reflect the arrangement silently lapsing rather than anyone reneging on it.","scope":"Household chore coordination"},{"id":"a3","type":"claim","text":"The friend's avoidance of the conversations is evidence that the conversations have become aversive; requiring attendance at more of the same conversations is likely to deepen the withdrawal. This is a conjecture, not an observed fact about that friend.","scope":"Interpretation of the avoiding friend"},{"id":"a4","type":"commitment","text":"Propose a short, explicit trial (e.g., two weeks) in which each chore agreement is recorded in a shared place with a named person, a done-criterion, and a time.","action":"Initiate a time-boxed written-agreement trial","consequence":"Disputes about meaning become checkable against a record rather than contested from memory.","depends":["a1","a2"]},{"id":"a5","type":"commitment","text":"Offer the avoiding friend an asynchronous, low-stakes channel — e.g., the shared note editable on their own time — and count their written input as full participation instead of requiring meeting attendance.","action":"Open an asynchronous input channel","depends":["a3"]},{"id":"a6","type":"commitment","text":"Raise the recurring pattern at a calm, scheduled moment rather than during an active dispute, and keep the friendship conversation separate from the chore-negotiation conversation.","action":"Hold one calm meta-conversation separated from incidents"},{"id":"a7","type":"objection","text":"Clarity alone may not resolve the disputes: once tasks are recorded, a genuine imbalance of effort may become visible, and the asker should be prepared to renegotiate the split itself, not merely its wording.","target":["a4"],"bearing":"Limits the claimed sufficiency of the written-agreement trial."},{"id":"a8","type":"problem","text":"Unresolved from the material: whether the arguments track real inequity or only divergent recollections; whether the avoiding friend also avoids doing chores; and what follows if even asynchronous coordination is refused — at which point the question shifts from chore management to the viability of the living arrangement."}],"uptake":["a4","a5","a6","a7"]}